Requisition ID:  98654 

Job Category:  Engineering; Infrastructure 

Location:  Pittsburgh, PA, United States 

Join a company that is passionately committed to the pursuit of a better world through positive change. With more than 70 years of business and technical expertise in mining , energy , and infrastructure , our 10,000 colleagues in 150 countries tirelessly work toward bettering the industries in which we operate. With practical solutions that are safe, innovative and sustainable, we think globally while acting locally. 

Join our Project Delivery Group (PDG), a dynamic team of professionals passionately committed to world-class  project delivery  across the globe. With expertise in sustainable studies, asset building and operations, and industry-leading efficiencies, our best-in-class team leverages methodologies, governance and systems that are unparalleled in the  engineering  space. Are you looking for an opportunity to join a diverse group of professionals who are committed to remaining exceptional? We look forward to hearing from you.

Hatch has an exciting career opportunity for an experienced Municipal Water & Wastewater Project Manager in Pittsburgh, PA. In this role, you will contribute to the leadership of the water group and support the technical direction of municipal water and wastewater infrastructure projects.

Responsibilities: 

Lead all phases of project management including: proposal development; client interaction and overall technical oversight of a project;

Conducts comprehensive engineering planning, design, and operational studies of water and wastewater utilities systems, including stormwater management and “green” sustainable infrastructure technology applications;

Prepare project bidding documents for municipal water and wastewater projects including plans, specifications, cost estimates and schedules;

Determine design criteria in accordance with required standards and codes for assigned projects with water and wastewater utilities, including stormwater and “green” sustainable infrastructure;

Design of site developments, linear infrastructure and water and wastewater facilities, including: site grading, roads, water distribution, sanitary and storm sewer systems, stormwater management / drainage systems, and pump stations;

Review and check engineering drawings, plans, computations, estimates and reports for completeness, accuracy, and soundness of applied engineering principles and with standards and policies;

Provide guidance and work supervision for drafting designers and junior engineers as required by projects;

Client development and management to ensure project delivery successfully meets the needs of the Clients.

Qualifications: 

Bachelor’s degree in engineering from an accredited University;

Minimum of 10 years of engineering experience in water and wastewater infrastructure design projects;

Professional Engineer Registration in the State of Pennsylvania and the ability to obtain registration in other states through reciprocity;

Knowledge of civil and/or other engineering principles and techniques related to municipal engineering and water and wastewater utilities, stormwater management and “green” sustainable infrastructure technologies;

Ability to apply sound utility engineering principles to both operational and design issues;

Ability to write general and technical specifications, lead the development of project design drawings and prepare project bidding packages in an accurate and timely manner;

Ability to schedule design and construction projects, prepare engineering and construction cost estimates;

Ability to interpret national and local codes and standards to insure compliance;

Extensive people management skills including mentoring;

Demonstrable business development and planning experience;

Track record in a consultancy role with extensive exposure to client-facing work;

Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively; build relationships and influence effectively, with colleagues, clients and stakeholders;

Excellent communication, interpersonal and teamwork skills in complex and changing environments.

Why join us? 

Work with great people to make a difference

Collaborate on exciting projects to develop innovative solutions

Top employer 

What we offer you? 

Flexible work environment

Long term career development

Think globally, work locally

Don't meet every single requirement? You don't need to. At Hatch, we are building a diverse, inclusive workplace that fosters innovation. If you're interested in this role, we encourage you to apply even if your past experiences don't perfectly align with the skills we've listed.

We're committed to fostering a workforce that reflects the diversity of the communities in which we operate and serve. Hatch is an Equal Opportunity Employer that considers applicants without regard to age, race, color, national origin, citizenship, religion, creed, gender, sexual orientation, marital status, disability, veteran, or any other protected status. If you have any accommodation requirements, please let us know. We'll do our best to meet your needs in accordance with applicable local legislation.

Nearest Major Market: Pittsburgh

Job Segment: 
 Project Manager, Wastewater, Drafting, Water Treatment, Architecture, Technology, Engineering

What if you could do the kind of work the world needs?

At WSP, you can access our global scale, contribute to landmark projects and connect with the brightest minds in your field to do the best work of your life. You can embrace your curiosity in a culture that celebrates new ideas and diverse perspectives. You can experience a world of opportunity and the chance to shape a career as unique as you.

This role will see you enhance your capabilities and the reputation of WSP’s Building Structures team. You will collaborate with talented professionals working on iconic projects to drive future ready outcomes that will benefit clients and communities.

Our WSP Building Structures group are a specialist team renowned for their innovation in structural engineering and cutting-edge BIM project execution across high-rise and complex building structures and infrastructure projects, with offices in every major city across Australia.

We operate as a highly autonomous and genuinely national team. The ability to grow and develop your career at WSP are unparalleled in the market. We offer the opportunity to contribute to local and national buildings projects, plus the ability to expand your design skills across other market sectors.

Our recent projects span across a range of different sectors including but not limited to high-rise developments, schools, infrastructure, the list goes on. Some of our recent projects include:

- City Tattersalls Club Redevelopment

- Sydney Fish Market

- Sydney Harbourside

- Shellharbour Hospital

- 2 Chifley Square

At WSP you’ll find the scale and reach you need to do the kind of work the world needs – and the culture and people that make it the best work of your life.

What you’ll do

- Project lead work across the design, delivery and tender phases for multi-year/packaged work for turnkey projects;

- Ensure timely and quality of delivery for project and structural engineering work in support of relevant technical, commercial and regulatory standards – and in alignment with schedules and budgets;

- Provide practical engineering advice and recommendations relating to site compliance and construction outcomes;

- Handle ongoing communication and highly effective professional relationships with local clients;

- Manage effective stakeholder relationships, both internally and externally;

- Mentor, train and develop the careers of junior engineers;

- Partner with internal stakeholders and a collaborative, national team in a multidisciplinary engineering setting;

Skills & Required Experience

- Bachelor to Masters’ level degree in Civil/Structural Engineering;

- 4-10 years industry  experience in Australia on building projects in the commercial, retail, defence, health or education sectors;

- Solid proficiency in all-round structural engineering design including post-tensioned concrete;

- Track record of effective cross-discipline project delivery;

- Strong communication skills and the ability to engage confidently with site personnel and clients;

- The ability to lead, train and mentor junior engineers across technical and project delivery aspects;

- Naturally Curious, Passionate, Adaptable & ready to do the kind of work the world needs;

Imagine a better future for you and a better future for us all.

Join our close-knit community of talented individuals who share your passion for making a positive impact. Our global team includes more than 80,000 employees, working together to make a difference in communities both close to home and around the world.

An employee Share Purchase Plan is available to all our permanent employees who wish to become owners and vested partners in WSP’s collective success. To find out more about our commitment to the health and wellbeing of our people, and the programs we’ve designed to help you thrive, go to our Employee Benefits page.

- Develop your professional network (locally, nationally and globally) through various initiatives.

- Develop your personal brand through targeted training.

- Develop your business understanding and awareness through various procedures.

WSP prioritises the health and wellbeing of our people by offering flexible working, 12 months parental leave, opportunities for global mobility, purchased additional leave, and competitive remuneration among many more benefits designed to help you shine.

We are committed to providing an inclusive, diverse and equal opportunity workplace. We promote Indigenous voices and are actively delivering a ‘Stretch’ level Reconciliation Action Plan. Accredited by the Workplace Gender Equality Agency as an Employer of Choice, we also support the LGBTQI+ community, and encourage all employees to bring their whole selves to work.

With us, you can. Apply today.

